When Gym Equipment Becomes Furniture.
@alamastudio_ is rethinking what fitness equipment can look like. Instead of treating weights and machines as objects to hide away, the Italian brand designs them as permanent pieces of architecture, crafted with the same attention to materiality, proportion and detail as collectible furniture.
Designed by Lorenzo Arnold and founded by Gabriele Zanni and Andrea Sacco, every piece is manufactured in Italy using 316L stainless steel, solid ALPI wood and premium Italian leather. The result is a collection that feels equally at home in a Brutalist villa, a Milanese apartment or aboard a superyacht, dissolving the boundary between wellness and interior design.
Rather than dominating a room, Alama’s equipment becomes part of it. Sculptural dumbbells, benches and wall-mounted storage systems are conceived as design objects first, proving that performance and craftsmanship don’t have to exist separately. In Alama’s world, working out is no longer confined to the gym, it becomes another expression of the spaces we choose to live in.
